  "goodToKnow": "Der Darm is the intestine, with the plural Därme. The two parts are der Dünndarm (small intestine) and der Dickdarm (large intestine), and die Darmflora is the gut flora. Der Blinddarm is the caecum, but Germans use it for the appendix too: Blinddarmentzündung means appendicitis. Eine Darmspiegelung is a colonoscopy. Darm is also the casing of natural sausages, der Naturdarm."
